// name :
"P857397029" "Devil Take the Hindmost"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DeskClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2442767935" "Heavily Censored Memo"
// DetailString :
"P4010164838" "This memo is from the Rhode Island Department of Corrections, but most of the key references are blacked out. It refers to construction of some sort of facility, but it's unclear where the facility was built or for what purpose."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CabinetClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P994715718" "Irate Letter"
// DetailString :
"P3245283019" "This letter appears to have been written a U.S. Senator from the 1940s. He appears concerned with a 'Project Marduk', and the secrecy surrounding it. He also refers to anonymous 'private partners', and requests their identities. Given that you found the letter amongst other discarded and ignored mail, you can only assume that his requests were denied."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SafeClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1544336196" "Facility Blueprints"
// DetailString :
"P3291164366" "You found a series of blueprints for what looks like a prison, though large sections of it appear to be missing. The blueprints were accompanied by a cryptic letter referring to a company named Milestone Labs, SPC. The letter seemed to indicate that unknown tech was being integrated into the prison's construction."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - PandorasBoxVillainArc3Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P978500819" "Zigursky Blueprints"
// tDetailString :
"P175744146" "These blueprints are what finally led you to Pandora's Box. It was a race against Arachnos, the Freedom Phalanx, and anyone else that wanted to get their hands on the power of the gods, and...<br><br><color gold><b>Devil Take the Hindmost</b></color><br><br>It began with a personal request from Doctor Harvan. He wanted you to investigate an abandoned government office on the outskirts of Paragon City. His interest was in the fate of his late father, but what you found was cryptic information about a prison built in the 1950s.<br><br>As you were about to leave, you encountered Captain Mako, who had been tasked with trailing your movements. You defeated Mako, and then made him an offer: he could play double agent for you, while maintaining his position inside Arachnos. Mako was noncommittal, but he seemed open to the idea.<br><br>When you returned to Harvan with your findings, it quickly became clear that something was missing from the picture... and that something, you deduced, was likely the very artifact you were looking for. When Lastri learned of your findings, she immediately set into motion a plan: attack Talos Island, simultaneously diverting enemy attention while giving your infamy a significantly more urgent quality. You wreaked some havoc and took down the Freedom Phalanx's newest member, Penelope Yin.<br><br>With your name in all of the papers in Paragon, it was a simple task to get admitted to the Zig. You turned yourself in to the Paragon Police Department, who immediately shipped you to exactly where you needed to be. Inside the Zig, your powers were marginalized, but you managed to get by on your wits. Odysseus created a distraction for you, and you nabbed the Antikythera from the prison guard's stash. With the Antikythera in hand, your powers were restored - and not a moment too soon, given that Harvan had led Citadel to your very location.<br><br>You took out a surprised Citadel and gave Harvan a piece of your mind, but you were eager to get to the task at hand. You blew a hole in the bottom of the Zig, exposing a path down to the abandoned labs below.<br><br>Underneath Zigursky, you found what you were looking for: Pandora's Box. However, proximity to Pandora's Box set off a reaction in Captain Castillo, causing him to go berserk and attack you. Seeing your fight with Castillo, Harvan determined that the Box itself was causing his instability, and made to open it.<br><br>Unfortunately, rather than granting its power to those nearby, Pandora's Box exploded, releasing creatures of pure energy. You managed to fight them off long enough to allow Lastri to swoop in and grant your escape."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - HarvanTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P2332178649" "Ah, {HeroName}. Just the {Hero.gender=male man|woman} I wanted to see. I have a request for you. It is, ah...<br><br><color orange>Harvan looks at his feet, shifting nervously. After a short breath, he raises his eyes to meet your gaze.</color><br><br>It is of a... somewhat personal nature."
// Answer Text :
"P530313632" "Alright... what's your request, then?"
// Answer Text :
"P2590988851" "Stick to your work, Harvan. You're here to help find Pandora's Box."
// Page Hostile Text :
"P267581372" "Well, that's just the thing, {HeroName}. What I'm about to ask of you is, in fact, quite closely related to the search for Pandora's Box.<br><br>It... it involves my father, and his work. I'm still using the Antikythera to try to pinpoint the Box's location, but it takes time to interpret the readings. I believe that this task may speed the process somewhat, depending on what you find."
// Answer Text :
"P86716640" "Alright, Harvan... this better be good."
// Page Request Text :
"P188805009" "My father, Sir Isaiah Harvan, dedicated most of his life to the search for Pandora's Box. I have taken up his quest myself, and we've arguably come much closer to finding it than my father ever did.<br><br><color orange>Harvan's brow furrows, and he pauses a moment before speaking again.</color><br><br>However... it is his untimely disappearance that I would like to speak with you about. My father's research has led me to many things, including the existence of the Antikythera. In his later years, he became convinced that someone within the United States government knew more about Pandora's Box than they let on, and his investigation became significantly more... political."
// Answer Text :
"P1781996194" "Meaning, he drew the attention of some dangerous people."
// Page Request2 Text :
"P15523569" "<color orange>Harvan nods at you.</color><br><br>Exactly. He was pursuing this very avenue of investigation right up until the day he disappeared. Obviously, those of us close to him suspected foul play, but... well, you know how these things go. When an eccentric explorer that believes in the myths of ancient Greece disappears, it doesn't exactly make the front page.<br><br>Still, I believe my father was onto something significant, and it is my belief that you are... <i>less susceptible</i> to harm than my father was."
// Answer Text :
"P457330896" "So, you want me to pick up where he left off."
// Page Request3 Text :
"P3951104878" "I believe it would serve both our interests, {HeroName}. It could provide us with vital information on Pandora's Box... and it could also uncover my father's fate.<br><br>I won't hide the fact that I have a personal stake in this... but I also believe it's the best place to look, given our situation."
// Answer Text :
"P2774932237" "Alright, Harvan. I'll look into it."
// Page NotTaskOwner Text :
"P2620207394" "<color skyblue>Only the team leader can cause the mission to progress through dialogue."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DeskTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P3458233036" "<color orange>You search through the desk, looking for any documents of interest. The few papers you find are old and soiled, not to mention completely unreadable.<br><br>Upon testing the drawers, you find more of the same: extremely old office supplies and refuse. One of the drawers, however, appears to be locked..."
// Answer Text :
"P863232310" "(Break the lock on the drawer)"
// Page Desk1 Text :
"P1446471307" "<color orange>Using your unique capabilities, you manage to bypass the lock on the drawer, taking care not to damage the contents in the process.<br><br>Inside, you find copious amounts of dust... but you also spot a large manila envelope that appears to have been moderately well-preserved.<br><br>Inside the envelope are a series of official-looking documents, each of which appears to be quite liberally censored."
// Answer Text :
"P4169575293" "(Inspect the documents)"
// Page Desk2 Text :
"P680453136" "<color orange>Most of these are either unintelligible or mundane, but one document in particular catches your eye:<br><br><color skyblue>OFFICE OF THE RHODE ISLAND DEPARTMENT OF CORRECTIONS<br><br><br><br>MEMORANDUM TO:     Administrator, Corrections Facility Research & Development<br><br>SUBJECT:     Project <color black>REDACTED</color><br><br>While your concerns are understandable and noted, the primary funding partners for Project <color black>REDACTED</color> will remain classified for the time being. Rest assured that the RIDC has strict security measures in place for the facility, and that site construction is being overseen by both public and private personnel. Continue development for the <color black>REDACTED</color> facility as previously planned.<br><br>We are currently operating under a strict timetable, and unless <color black>REDACTED</color> is completed on schedule, construction will need to be put on hold. As you are aware, the longer construction takes, the more involved local authorities will become. If you require more resources to complete <color black>REDACTED</color> on schedule, speak with Comptroller <color black>REDACTED</color>.<br><br>Enclosure<br><color black>REDACTED</color><br><br><color orange>In the margins of the memo, in scrawled handwriting, is the following message:<br><br></color>Senator - this is the best that I could get. I know it's not much. I may be able to get more if you can put some pressure on the Board.<br><br>-Ron"
// Answer Text :
"P2385719541" "(Leave)"
// Page TaskComplete Text :
"P82647379" "<color orange>There doesn't appear to be anything more of interest here."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - CabinetTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P2898244222" "<color orange>Amongst the discarded remains of the small office, you find a file cabinet that appears to have survived mostly intact. The drawers inside are filled with dividers and documents of varying conditions."
// Answer Text :
"P3984258674" "(Begin sifting through the documents)"
// Page Cabinet1 Text :
"P3720292640" "<color orange>While most of these documents appear to be unmarred by government censors, they also appear to be mostly useless. After sifting through some irate letters from the Brickstown Business Association and angry, error-ridden screeds about UFOs, you come to realize that you're looking at a collection of incoming mail.<br><br>Just as you're ready to give up and move on, a distinctly official-looking letter catches your eye..."
// Answer Text :
"P2989653162" "(Read the letter)"
// Page Cabinet2 Text :
"P1010198297" "<color skyblue>Senator James S. Neill<br>Chairman, Senate Judiciary Committee<br>United States Senate<br>Washington, DC 20510<br>May 10, 1949<br><br>Supervisor Tornay:<br><br>I am deeply troubled by your department's reluctance to forward pertinent information on 'Project Marduk'. While I fully understand that major components of the facility are proprietary, it is not generally the practice of Congress to fund projects without knowing the recipient of those funds.<br><br>I can understand if you wish to maintain Classified status on the technology behind the project, but you must at least divulge the <i>identity</i> of all private partners involved in the project. Using unknown tech in a government facility is one thing, Supervisor, but receiving said tech from an unknown party without disclosing <i>any</i> related information is simply ludicrous.<br><br>I shall await your prompt reply. I hope that a subpoena will not be necessary in this instance.<br><br>Sincerely,<br><br>James S. Neill<br>United States Senator, MO"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - SafeTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P3150403155" "<color orange>This safe stands out as one of the only highly-secured objects you've seen here. If there's anything left in this building that might be of interest to you, it's probably in here."
// Answer Text :
"P245401896" "(Attempt to pry open the safe)"
// Page Safe1 Text :
"P1982100606" "<color orange>The lock looks to be in a state of significant disrepair, and with some careful manipulation, you manage to pry the rusted door open.<br><br>Inside, you find a set of blueprints for a high-security prison. As you flip through the blueprints, you note that they appear to be incomplete - many of the connections to the lower levels of the prison seem to link elsewhere, but are simply labeled '<color skyblue>subcontract</color>'.<br><br>At the back of the pile, you find a one-page summary of interaction with an organization called Milestone Labs, SPC."
// Answer Text :
"P1419082505" "(Read through the summary)"
// Page Safe2 Text :
"P1638476671" "<color skyblue>OFFICE OF THE UNITED STATES METAHUMAN INTELLIGENCE PROTOCOL<br><br><br><br>MEMORANDUM TO:     Supervisor, Corrections Facility Administration & Construction<br><br>SUBJECT:     Project Marduk<br><br>The contract with Milestone Labs, SPC has been written up. We're still working on the fine details, but your department can begin construction plans immediately.<br><br>Unfortunately, negotiations regarding patent rights and proprietary transparency have not been successful. The boys at Milestone are insistent that they maintain total control over their tech, even as it's applied to Project Marduk. I don't like it, but frankly, this project doesn't get off the ground unless we use them.<br><br>Research into alternative methods of containing powered entities is still underway, but this project has stalled long enough. Run up some new plans, under the assumption that inmates will be able to generate no more than 100kN. That should bring the project well within budget.<br><br>Enclosure<br>Roger S. Vrabel<br>Senior Director, Metahuman Intelligence Protocol<br><br>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MakoTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P733557454" "<color orange>After the beating you gave him, Mako appears to be having some trouble breathing. His gills are opening and closing violently, and his every breath comes out as a loud rasp.<br><br>In his current state, he seems to be unable to communicate... it looks like you'll need to do the talking, here."
// Answer Text :
"P1301281951" "Mako. Can you hear me?"
// Page Mako1 Text :
"P3044228318" "<color orange>Mako continues to focus almost entirely on continuing to breathe, but he takes the effort to look up at you. Your eyes lock with his, and you can see defiance and anger in the stare he gives you."
// Answer Text :
"P487316604" "Don't give me that look, Mako. I haven't killed you... yet."
// Answer Text :
"P2257149963" "Arachnos sent you to follow me, right? How's that going?"
// Page Mako2 Text :
"P2622707423" "<color orange>Mako flinches at your words. With some effort, he manages to get out a ragged attempt at communication.</color><br><br>What... *hrrrrkkkk*...<br><br>What do you... want... *hrrrrrrrrrkkkkkkkk*..."
// Answer Text :
"P2786673803" "I'm recruiting, Mako. I'm sure word has gotten out."
// Page Mako3 Text :
"P338224271" "<color orange>Mako manages a grin at you, filled with rows of jagged teeth. He closes his eyes, and shakes his head.</color><br><br>Not... *hrrrkkkk*... switching sides..."
// Answer Text :
"P1673465502" "Why play just one? I need someone on the inside."
// Page Mako4 Text :
"P2810283941" "<color orange>Mako's breathing has steadied now. He looks thoughtful... for a shark.</color><br><br>What do you have to offer... *hrrkk*... that Recluse can't? Arachnos rules the Isles, {HeroName}... and when we get Pandora's Box, it's all over. No one will be able to stop us."
// Answer Text :
"P3284249269" "Arachnos is in decline, and you know it. What's your exit strategy?"
// Answer Text :
"P3928623412" "But I'm always a step ahead, Mako. What happens when I get the Box?"
// Page Mako5 Text :
"P1759731583" "<color orange>Mako ponders this for a moment.</color><br><br>I'll... consider it, {HeroName}. I don't take Recluse lightly, but...<br><br><color orange>Mako looks up at you again. This time, the anger and defiance appear to be mingled with... at least some level of respect.</color><br><br>But I don't think I can take you lightly, either."
// Answer Text :
"P479944509" "Think it over, then. I have places to be."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - HarvanEndTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P517726361" "{HeroName}! I think I've made a breakthrough. By comparing readings from the Antikythera at different locations, I was able to triangulate a pattern in the energy flows in this area. Based on the trajectories I've witnessed, I'd surmise that-"
// Answer Text :
"P1530710089" "Harvan..."
// Page HarvanEnd1 Text :
"P1796779666" "<color orange>Harvan seems not to hear you.</color><br><br>...but the patterns were all wrong, you see. If they moved elliptically, their origin point would have been somewhere in Michigan, which I <i>knew</i> to be false. But then, it hit me. The streams don't act like particles of light, but like <i>jets of air</i>. They're limited by geographical constraints! Factoring this data, I managed to-"
// Answer Text :
"P904117100" "Harvan!"
// Page HarvanEnd2 Text :
"P1341618274" "...almost like magnets! They're <i>drawn</i> to large populations, specifically of humans! After applying this modification to my equations, I was able to calculate their trajectories with significantly greater precision! I'm now confident that-"
// Answer Text :
"P2153124396" "DOCTOR HARVAN!"
// Page HarvanEnd3 Text :
"P2428200158" "<color orange>Raising your voice seems to have gotten his attention. Harvan trails off, staring at you vacantly for a moment. He shakes his head roughly, as if waking from a trance.</color><br><br>I'm... sorry, {HeroName}. I suppose I got a little too excited there. Did you... find something of interest?"
// Answer Text :
"P1606806034" "As a matter of fact, I did."
// Page HarvanEnd4 Text :
"P2559718503" "<color orange>You relate the events of your investigation to Harvan, and hand him the documents you found. As he pores over them, he grows increasingly confused.</color><br><br>What...<br><br>What is this? I recognize this design. I've seen it before...<br><br><color orange>Harvan's brows furrow.</color><br><br>This is... this is the design for Zigursky Penitentiary."
// Answer Text :
"P3806316542" "It appears so."
// Page HarvanEnd5 Text :
"P657723716" "But this doesn't make any sense. Why would my father care about this? His research never involved modern structures, and he certainly wasn't interested in the political machinations of the United States...<br><br>Besides, these designs are deeply flawed. This structure might be suitable for common criminals, or perhaps minor villains, but... there's no way these designs could contain metahumans of any significant scale.<br><br><color orange>Harvan's eyes widen, and he looks up at you.</color><br><br>Unless..."
// Answer Text :
"P4114717179" "Unless something was limiting their powers."
// Page HarvanEnd6 Text :
"P3997073636" "<color orange>Harvan's hands begin to tremble with excitement.</color><br><br>Something... something that could limit the powers of any metahuman. Something that unified the concepts of science and magic, of technological progress and natural prowess.<br><br>Something that commanded the very essence of power itself."
// Answer Text :
"P490462614" "You mean, something like Pandora's Box."
// Page HarvanEnd7 Text :
"P1604293760" "This fits with all of my findings, {HeroName}. If our theory is correct, then... <i>someone</i> has been utilizing Pandora's Box as a sort of safeguard against metahuman criminals. It's a crude use of such a powerful artifact, but...<br><br><color orange>Harvan trials off.</color>We need to inform the others of your findings. If we're correct, we'll need to set up an expedition right away."
// Answer Text :
"P4218168415" "Agreed. I'll set up a meeting."

